WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:13.139
In this lesson, you will learn to use “ask and wait” and the answer reporter to personalise a story and let the reader choose what happens next.

2
00:00:13.739 --> 00:00:18.887
“ask and wait” shows a question and a typing box.

3
00:00:18.887 --> 00:00:24.035
The script waits until the reader types and presses enter.

4
00:00:24.635 --> 00:00:30.217
Whatever the reader typed is stored in the blue “answer” reporter.

5
00:00:30.217 --> 00:00:35.800
Join it to other words to use it in a sentence.

6
00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:44.157
Use if-else with the answer to make the story branch: different answers lead to different scenes.

7
00:00:44.757 --> 00:00:51.209
Never ask readers for private information like their address, phone number or school.

8
00:00:51.209 --> 00:00:55.487
A first name or a choice is enough.

9
00:00:56.087 --> 00:00:59.930
Great work! Let’s remember what we learned.

10
00:00:59.930 --> 00:01:05.078
Now build along, then try the challenges. You’ve got this!
